From 74a7bce2057910373f9a400771f993f09e8bc263 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:06:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban sync: a failed pre-pull push still pulls;
 outbox alarm ages only sendable ops; repin pulls under the board lock; sync
 diff moves nothing

Follow-ups to PR #1934 (push before pull) from its exact-head reviews 5888384602 and 5892044920
(card t_01a1d41c2612ebc0).

1. A transport error (HubError/OSError) on the push before the pulls no longer skips them. With the
   Board's /ops down and /changes up the replica pulled 0 of 3 remote rows; now the pulls run, the
   send after them retries, and its failure fails the round (a board still behind is noted for an
   immediate rerun before re-raising).
2. Outbox-age alarm while behind the feed head ages exactly what push(before_head=True) would send:
   kanban_sync_outbox_age.sendable_age_s runs kanban_sync_backlog.sendable_before_head over push's own
   selection, with the latest round's Board reads and no Board call of its own. The FIFO tail after the
   first pending task_runs row and stale wakes held for cards the Board completed no longer WARN or
   file the stalled-outbox card during a long catch-up; a sendable op still alarms.
3. kanban_worker_repin pulls the live board only under board_sync_lock, taken without waiting (as
   dispatch_tick): while a round holds it the read-back reports pending (the round applies the row) and a
   CAS retry re-checks the file and CASes again only at a newer revision. When the bounded pull stops at
   its page budget before the repinned row, a targeted row_evidence read applies the card's Board row like
   a push's merged row (cursor unchanged), so a >20-page backlog still confirms the CAS (and a conflict
   retry sees the newest revision).
4. `sync diff` refreshes the replica as a diagnostic: no rebuild on Resync (reported as refresh_error,
   as before #1934) and no attachment transfers.
5. One Board read (row_evidence) per card per round: both sends share the round's cache, so a behind
   round reads N held cards N times, not 2N; the send after the pulls at the head reads none. The send
   before the pulls must still read: only its pull can tell an at-head round (the incident slept from
   the head).
6. sendable_before_head docstring: a held row holds that card's later tasks rows (key is table + uid).

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_round_followups.py, 13 tests, 11 RED on origin/main
(behavioural assertions), all GREEN. 151 test files importing the touched modules (all
test_kanban_sync*.py included): 3269 passed, 0 failed. scripts/check --base origin/main: ok.
